{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q014_paper_example_reclassification_pa1492","answer":"The current SCOPe stable release reported by the API is 2.08. In SCOP 1.69, PA1492 (1t1j chains A/B; d1t1ja_ and d1t1jb_) was classified as c.137.1.1: its own family and superfamily in the separate “Hypothetical protein PA1492” fold c.137. Nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase (1f8y chains A/B) was c.23.14.1, the N-deoxyribosyltransferase family within superfamily c.23.14 and the flavodoxin-like fold c.23. Thus, although both were in the alpha/beta class, SCOP 1.69 did not place them in the same fold or imply homology.

In SCOPe 2.08, the PA1492 core (residues 1–118 in each chain; d1t1ja1/d1t1jb1, retaining domain sunids 106249/106250) is reclassified as c.23.14.2. It now shares the flavodoxin-like fold c.23 and the N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like superfamily c.23.14 with 1f8y, while remaining in a distinct PA1492 family (.2 rather than the N-deoxyribosyltransferase family .1). This upgrades the relationship from merely sharing the broad alpha/beta class to probable remote common ancestry at superfamily strength—not close family-level homology. Both crystallographic copies support the same result, so it is not an artifact of choosing chain A as a representative; SCOPe separately labels short non-core/tag segments of 1t1j as artifacts (l.1.1.1).

The reclassification makes 1f8y a reasonable structural/superfamily template for PA1492’s core fold, but it does not justify transferring the nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase function, catalytic residues, or substrate specificity to PA1492. Such transfer would require independent sequence/active-site evidence and biochemical functional evidence.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1t1j","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1f8y","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1f8y/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1f8ya_","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/106249","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/31395","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/106249","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/31395","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110463","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52312","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110463","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52312","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110462","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52311","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110462","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52311","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110461","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52310","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110461","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52310","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110460","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52309","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52309","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/110459","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sunids/52171","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52171"]}]}
